    {
      "week": 43,
      "slug": "shuffling-picture-cards",
      "title": "Shuffling picture cards",
      "idea": "A six-story shuffle bijection works, while a plausible wrong-range swap rule has biased outputs.",
      "gates": "K-1: positional language, matching and enacted swaps. Grades 2-3: organize six stories. Grades 4-5: equal-weight choices, division or sharing into equal piles; distinguish fixed histories from random distributions.",
      "materials": "Three distinct same-size picture cards, three-slot strips, cups and numbered tickets. Keep a second card set for comparing starts; extra-card extensions may stay on paper.",
      "pretest": "Test self-swaps and the ticket reset. After the first swap, replace the cup contents with tickets 2 and 3, including any ticket just drawn. Reset all three between full shuffles.",
