    {
      "week": 44,
      "slug": "copying-bag",
      "title": "The bag that copies",
      "idea": "Returning and copying a draw creates dependent stories but an exact uniform distribution of red-draw totals.",
      "gates": "K-1: count to six, match colors and follow an adult-read question. Grades 2-3: distinguish marked counter identities over two draws. Grades 4-5: branching counts and small products; factorial notation is optional.",
      "materials": "Opaque bags or cups, five counters of each color per pair, identity labels, trays and pencils. Only one counter of each color begins inside; extras stay outside.",
      "pretest": "Demonstrate returning the same counter before adding its copy. Reset to the two original counters between stories. Identity-label digits record birth steps, not color totals.",
