    {
      "week": 45,
      "slug": "visible-hidden-sides",
      "title": "The visible side",
      "idea": "Conditioning on a visible color requires counting eligible faces; changing the chooser changes the answer.",
      "gates": "All groups: match two-sided objects, sort cases by a clue and count small sets. Grades 2-3 compare chooser rules. Grades 4-5 characterize fair ticket subsets and diagnose information leaks. Fractions are optional.",
      "materials": "Opaque two-sided RR, RB and BB cards with six numbered faces, six same-size tickets, a cup, screen and identical opaque number covers. Use R/B labels as well as color.",
      "pretest": "Check that only color is revealed: hide ticket, face number, card identity and reverse-side printing. Added blue-showing rounds are set aside when comparing a red clue. This handling test is unperformed.",
