    {
      "week": 46,
      "slug": "forgetting-boards",
      "title": "Two boards forget their starts",
      "idea": "Shared assignments erase a board's initial state, while shared toggles preserve disagreements.",
      "gates": "All groups: left-to-right slots and color matching. Grades 2-3: track visited positions and changed rules. Grades 4-5: compare eight board states and equal-weight choices; fractions are optional.",
      "materials": "Two three-slot strips per pair, reversible R/B counters or replacement squares, six slot-color tickets, cups and visited-slot markers.",
      "pretest": "Rehearse setting versus toggling: setting may leave a color unchanged; toggling changes it. Return and mix random tickets each time. Coverage occurs eventually with probability one, with no finite guaranteed draw count.",
